Our end-of-the-semester (Spring 2018) lab gathering was held over lunch at noon in Allbritton 304.

At that session, we heard a bit of what the lab’s been doing—especially from the pilot ‘Roads of the Middle Ages’ project—and from our guest Professor [Emilia Jamroziak of Leeds University](https://ahc.leeds.ac.uk/history/staff/863/professor-emilia-jamroziak) who talked briefly at lunch on the topic,  
“**Working with Networks Regionally and Comparatively: How to Do it Safely and Sensibly**.”

